{title: Last of the Princes}
{subtitle: Numbers 1:15; 1:42–43; 2:29–30; 7:78–83; 10:27}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 94}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×12

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From the camp on the north side
Ahira son of Enan stands
The banner of Dan is near
Where the tribe of Naphtali lands
Fif-ty-three thousand men
Listed by name and clan
Fit for battle they stand
Under the starry canopy
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the twelfth day he [B]comes
[F#]With the offering of the [C#]last prince
Sil[D#m]ver plates and gold [B]dish
In the [F#]tabernacle of [C#]God
This was the [D#m]offering [B]
Of A[F#]hira son of E[C#]nan [D#m]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
When the wilderness broke camp
The rear guard moves along
Ahira leads the division
Where the north wind blows strong
Two oxen and five rams
Five male lambs a year old
Sin offering and burnt offering
Laid upon the holy ground
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the twelfth day he [B]comes
[F#]With the offering of the [C#]last prince
Sil[D#m]ver plates and gold [B]dish
In the [F#]tabernacle of [C#]God
This was [D#m]the offering [B]
Of A[F#]hira son of E[C#]nan
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |
| [D#m] | [B] | [F#] | [C#] | ×2
| [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] | [D#m] |

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Son of Enan he was
Chief of Naphtali's band
Faithful in his charge
Until the journey ends
{end_of_verse}
